{
 "cells": [
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["# Synthetic Credit Card Fraud Detection Scorecard\n","\n","This notebook builds a compact, explainable demo from **synthetic data only**. It combines transaction velocity (time since the previous transaction) with amount relative to an account's previous-transaction baseline. Flags are for review, not proof of fraud.\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n","from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score, roc_curve, confusion_matrix, classification_report\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n","from sklearn.pipeline import make_pipeline\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n","\n","RANDOM_STATE = 42\n","rng = np.random.default_rng(RANDOM_STATE)\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 1. Generate fake transactions\n","Each account gets a typical spending level. A small subset of generated transactions are synthetic anomalies: unusually large amounts occurring shortly after the account's prior transaction. Names are fictional labels for the demo only.\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["rows = []\n","base_time = pd.Timestamp('2026-01-01 00:00:00')\n","n_accounts = 250\n","\n","for account_num in range(n_accounts):\n","    account_id = f'ACCT-{account_num:04d}'\n","    account_name = f'Synthetic User {account_num:04d}'\n","    typical_amount = rng.uniform(20, 250)\n","    current_time = base_time + pd.Timedelta(minutes=int(rng.integers(0, 60 * 24)))\n","    n_txns = int(rng.integers(35, 65))\n","    for txn_num in range(n_txns):\n","        is_fraud = int(rng.random() < 0.035)\n","        if is_fraud:\n","            gap_minutes = float(rng.uniform(0.5, 5))\n","            amount = typical_amount * rng.uniform(4.0, 9.0)\n","        else:\n","            gap_minutes = float(rng.exponential(8 * 60) + 10)\n","            amount = float(rng.lognormal(np.log(typical_amount), 0.45))\n","        current_time += pd.Timedelta(minutes=gap_minutes)\n","        rows.append({\n","            'transaction_id': f'{account_id}-TXN-{txn_num:03d}',\n","            'account_id': account_id,\n","            'account_name': account_name,\n","            'transaction_time': current_time,\n","            'amount': round(float(amount), 2),\n","            'is_fraud': is_fraud,\n","        })\n","\n","transactions = pd.DataFrame(rows).sort_values(\n","    ['account_id', 'transaction_time', 'transaction_id']\n,").reset_index(drop=True)\n","transactions.head()"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["print(f'{len(transactions):,} transactions across {transactions.account_id.nunique():,} synthetic accounts')\n","print(f'Synthetic positive rate: {transactions.is_fraud.mean():.2%}')\n","transactions[['amount']].describe().round(2)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 2. Engineer the two risk signals\n","The baseline uses only the prior 30 transactions for that account (current transaction excluded), avoiding direct use of the current amount in its own baseline.\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["grouped = transactions.groupby('account_id', sort=False)\n","transactions['seconds_since_previous'] = grouped['transaction_time'].diff().dt.total_seconds()\n","transactions['prior_30_avg_amount'] = grouped['amount'].transform(\n","    lambda s: s.shift(1).rolling(window=30, min_periods=5).mean()\n,")\n","transactions['amount_to_baseline_ratio'] = (\n","    transactions['amount'] / transactions['prior_30_avg_amount'].replace(0, np.nan)\n",")\n","transactions[['seconds_since_previous', 'amount_to_baseline_ratio']] = (\n","    transactions[['seconds_since_previous', 'amount_to_baseline_ratio']].replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\n",")\n","\n","# This transparent rule is a review flag, with configurable example thresholds.\n","GAP_THRESHOLD_SECONDS = 10 * 60\n","AMOUNT_SPIKE_RATIO = 3.0\n","transactions['rule_flag'] = (\n","    transactions['seconds_since_previous'].le(GAP_THRESHOLD_SECONDS)\n","    & transactions['amount_to_baseline_ratio'].ge(AMOUNT_SPIKE_RATIO)\n").astype(int)\n","\n","model_data = transactions.dropna(subset=['seconds_since_previous', 'amount_to_baseline_ratio']).copy()\n","model_data[['transaction_time', 'amount', 'seconds_since_previous', 'prior_30_avg_amount', 'amount_to_baseline_ratio', 'rule_flag', 'is_fraud']].head(10)"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["print('Rule-flag rate:', f\"{model_data.rule_flag.mean():.2%}\")\n","print('Rule precision among flagged:', f\"{model_data.loc[model_data.rule_flag.eq(1), 'is_fraud'].mean():.2%}\" if model_data.rule_flag.any() else 'No rows flagged')\n","print('Rule recall:', f\"{model_data.loc[model_data.is_fraud.eq(1), 'rule_flag'].mean():.2%}\")\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 3. Fit a logistic-regression scorecard\n","We keep the two requested features interpretable. The split is stratified so both sets contain positive and negative examples.\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["FEATURES = ['seconds_since_previous', 'amount_to_baseline_ratio']\n","X = model_data[FEATURES].replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\n","y = model_data['is_fraud']\n","X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(\n","    X, y, test_size=0.25, random_state=RANDOM_STATE, stratify=y\n",")\n","\n","model = make_pipeline(\n","    StandardScaler(),\n","    LogisticRegression(class_weight='balanced', max_iter=1000, random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n,")\n","model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","test_scores = model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n","test_predictions = (test_scores >= 0.5).astype(int)\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["def ks_statistic(y_true, scores):\n","    \"\"\"Maximum gap between positive and negative empirical CDFs.\"\"\"\n","    fpr, tpr, _ = roc_curve(y_true, scores)\n","    return float(np.max(np.abs(tpr - fpr)))\n","\n","auc = roc_auc_score(y_test, test_scores)\n","gini = 2 * auc - 1\n","ks = ks_statistic(y_test, test_scores)\n","print(f'Test ROC-AUC: {auc:.3f}')\n","print(f'Test Gini:    {gini:.3f}')\n","print(f'Test KS:      {ks:.3f}')\n","print('\\nClassification report at illustrative 0.50 threshold:')\n","print(classification_report(y_test, test_predictions, digits=3, zero_division=0))\n","print('Confusion matrix [ [TN, FP], [FN, TP] ]:')\n","print(confusion_matrix(y_test, test_predictions))"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["fpr, tpr, _ = roc_curve(y_test, test_scores)\n","fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(12, 4.5))\n","axes[0].plot(fpr, tpr, label=f'AUC = {auc:.3f}')\n","axes[0].plot([0, 1], [0, 1], linestyle='--', color='gray')\n","axes[0].set(title='ROC curve (held-out synthetic data)', xlabel='False positive rate', ylabel='True positive rate')\n","axes[0].legend()\n","axes[1].hist(test_scores[y_test.to_numpy() == 0], bins=25, alpha=0.65, label='Synthetic non-fraud')\n","axes[1].hist(test_scores[y_test.to_numpy() == 1], bins=25, alpha=0.65, label='Synthetic fraud')\n","axes[1].set(title='Model score distributions', xlabel='Predicted score', ylabel='Transactions')\n","axes[1].legend()\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## 4. Example review queue\n","Rank the test examples for review. Scores are model outputs, **not calibrated probabilities of actual fraud**. Any final decision would need governed thresholds and human review.\n"]},
  {"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{},"outputs":[],"source":["review_queue = model_data.loc[X_test.index, [\n","    'transaction_id', 'account_id', 'transaction_time', 'amount',\n","    'seconds_since_previous', 'amount_to_baseline_ratio', 'rule_flag', 'is_fraud'\n,")].copy()\n","review_queue['model_score'] = test_scores\n","review_queue.sort_values('model_score', ascending=False).head(10).round(3)"]},
  {"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{},"source":["## Notes and limitations\n","- The labels are generated from the same broad pattern as the features, so strong results are expected and do not show real-world model quality.\n","- Real transaction data is sensitive. Never commit cardholder details, credentials, or proprietary data to a public repository.\n","- A fast repeat or unusual amount can have an innocent explanation. Alerts should support careful review, not automatic adverse action.\n","- Real use would require representative labelled data, leakage checks, threshold-cost analysis, fairness and compliance review, monitoring, access controls, and human oversight.\n","- The SQL equivalent is in `sql/feature_queries.sql`.\n"]}
 ],
